for days 0–4, so every plan runs short early. That doesn't change the ranking.\n4. **No major limits hit:** cash and the 288-unit warehouse don't seem to bind for any plan. Candidate 4 comes closest on space but appears to fit.\n\n**Order size relative to the demand forecast (product 0 / product 1)**\n\n| Candidate | Ordering frequency | Size vs. forecast |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3 | daily | ≈ 1.30 / 1.14 |\n| 7 | daily | ≈ 1.25 / 0.95 |\n| 2 | daily | ≈ 1.14 / 1.05 |\n| 6 | daily | ≈ 1.00 / 0.95 |\n| 5 | every other day | ≈ 1.25 / 1.10 |\n| 1 | every other day | ≈ 1.15 / 1.05 |\n| 0 | every other day | ≈ 1.05 / 0.95 |\n| 4 | every third day | ≈ 1.15 / 1.05 |\n\n**Ranking**\n- **Likely top:** 5, 3 and 1 are the most solid.\n- **Fourth place:** close between 4, 7 and 2.\n  - 7 orders product 1 below the forecast and pays daily fees.\n  - 2's sizes are only moderate.\n  - 4 saves on fees but pays more in storage.\n- **Likely bottom:** 0 and 6, which order at or below the forecast and so run short regularly."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4932, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4932}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T09:20:55.981Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWHFmrxPPSWsBbx52ED9"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JhgVzNmxgax37vUBxTJxtP", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-op